ic and natural gas infrastructure investments, which was partially offset by increased interest charges. The difference between GAAP and ongoing earnings was driven by recognition of customer refunds related to the 2023-2024 Prairie Island nuclear facility outage.</span></div><div style="margin-bottom:5pt;text-align:justify"><span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial Narrow',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-style:italic;font-weight:700;line-height:120%">SPS </span><span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial Narrow',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%">&#8212; GAAP and ongoing earnings increased $0.02 per share for the second quarter and $0.06 per share year-to-date. The year-to-date change was driven by sales growth and higher recovery of electric infrastructure investments, partially offset by increased depreciation expense.</span></div><div style="margin-bottom:5pt;text-align:justify"><span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial Narrow',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-style:italic;font-weight:700;line-height:120%">NSP-Wisconsin </span><span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial Narrow',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%">&#8212; GAAP and ongoing earnings increased $0.01 per share for the second quarter and $0.05 year-to-date. The year-to-date change was driven by higher recovery of electric and natural gas infrastructure investments, partially offset by increased depreciation expense and interest charges.</span></div><div style="margin-bottom:5pt;text-align:justify"><span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial Narrow',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-style:italic;font-weight:700;line-height:120%">Xcel Energy Inc. and Other </span><span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial Narrow',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%">&#8212; Primarily includes financing costs and interest income at the holding company and earnings from investment funds, which are accounted for as equity method investments.